t or present as a 'military technology during this time? Strictly choose an option from the unordered set {A, B}. A = present, B = absent"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Variable name: ditch\n"Variable description: The absence or presence of ditch as a military technology used in warfare.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "During the period from <time-start> to <time-end>, was the use of ditches as a military technology present or absent in the warfare strategies of '<polity>'? Strictly choose an option from the unordered set {A, B}. A = present, B = absent"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Variable name: chain\n"Variable description: The absence or presence of chainmail as a military technology used in warfare. We’re using a broad definition of chainmail. Habergeon was the word used to describe the Chinese version and that would qualify as chainmail. Armor that is made of small metal rings linked together in a pattern to form a mesh.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "During the period from <time-start> to <time-end>, was chainmail, defined as armor made of small metal rings linked together in a pattern to form a mesh, present or absent as a military technology in the warfare practices of '<polity>'? Strictly choose an option from the unordered set {A, B}. A = present, B = absent"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '"Variable name": Theological Syncretism Of Different Religions\n"Variable description": “Here we have to address the issue of the conversion of Vishnuvardhana from Jainism\xa0to Vaishnavism. It is not unreasonable to suppose that Ramanuja’s Vaishnava\xa0philosophy greatly influenced the cultural and religious history of not merely the\xa0Kannada region but Kerala as well. After it, Jain communities of Kannada region\xa0including the present Wayanad district of Kerala possibly divided into two groups and\xa0one began to profess Vaishnavism. But the ultimate result was the religious\xa0assimilation of these two groups. It is clearly evident from the Gowda communities of\xa0Wayanad region such as Vaishnava Gowda and Jain Gowdas. […] The\xa0 Janardhanagudi and\xa0 Vishnugudi Jain basties in Punchavayal near\xa0Panamaram are so confusing that it is difficult to distinguish them as either Jain or a\xa0Hindu Vishnu temple. The architectural and sculptural features of these temples\xa0indicate that they belong to twelfth century CE.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 921, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 811})
