chimec god-hero fusions (e.g., the familiar Quetzalcoatl and the cloud-serpent, Mixcoatl). Yet the principal deities were not gods in the Western sense; rather, they were divine complexes that could unfold into myriad aspects depending on specific temporal and spatial associations.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 890, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 774})
